    "id": "ppc-244",
    "statute": "Pakistan Penal Code 1860",
    "section": "244",
    "title": "Person employed in mint causing coin to be of different weight or composition from fixed law",
    "description": "Person employed in mint causing coin to be of different weight or composition from fixed law\n\nTHE PAKISTAN PENAL CODE, 1860\nTHE PAKISTAN PENAL CODE, 1860\nACT NO. XLV OF 1860.\nCHAPTER XII OF OFFENCES RELATING TO COINS AND GOVERNMENT STAMPS\n244. Person employed in mint causing coin to be different weight or composition from\nthat fixed by law. Whoever, being employed in any mint lawfully\nestablished in Pakistan, does any act, or omits what he is legally bound to do\nwith the intention of causing any coin issued from that mint to be of a\ndifferent weight or composition from the weight or composition fixed by law\nshall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may\nextend to seven years, and shall also be liable to fine.",
    "punishment": "shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may\nextend to seven years, and shall also be liable to fine.",
