    "description": "Altering appearance of Pakistan coin with intent that it shall pass as coin of different description\n\nTHE PAKISTAN PENAL CODE, 1860\nTHE PAKISTAN PENAL CODE, 1860\nACT NO. XLV OF 1860.\nCHAPTER XII OF OFFENCES RELATING TO COINS AND GOVERNMENT STAMPS\n249. Altering appearance of Pakistan coin\nwith intent that it shall pass as coin\nof different description. Whoever performs on any Pakistan coin any\noperation which alters the appearance of that coin with the intention that the\nsaid coin shall pass as a coin of a different description, shall be punished\nwith imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to seven\nyears, and shall also be liable to fine.",
