    "statute": "Pakistan Penal Code 1860",
    "section": "250",
    "title": "Delivery of coin possessed with knowledge that it is to be altered",
    "description": "Delivery of coin possessed with knowledge that it is to be altered\n\nTHE PAKISTAN PENAL CODE, 1860\nTHE PAKISTAN PENAL CODE, 1860\nACT NO. XLV OF 1860.\nCHAPTER XII OF OFFENCES RELATING TO COINS AND GOVERNMENT STAMPS\n250. Delivery of coin, possessed with knowledge that it is altered.\nWhoever, having coin in his possession with respect to which the offence defined\nin section 246 or 248 has been committed, and having known at the time when he\nbecame possessed of such coin that such offence had been committed with respect\nto it, fraudulently or with intent that fraud may be committed, delivers such\ncoin to any other person, or attempts to induce any other person to receive the\nsame shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which\nmay extend to five years, and shall also be liable to fine.",
