    "statute": "Pakistan Penal Code 1860",
    "section": "281",
    "title": "Exhibition of false light mark or buoy",
    "description": "Exhibition of false light mark or buoy\n\nTHE PAKISTAN PENAL CODE, 1860\nTHE PAKISTAN PENAL CODE, 1860\nACT NO. XLV OF 1860.\nCHAPTER XIV OF OFFENCES AFFECTING THE PUBLIC HEALTH SAFETY,\nCONVENIENCE, DECENCY AND MORALS\n281. Exhibition of false light, mark or\nbuoy. Whoever exhibits any false light mark or buoy intending or knowing it\nto be likely that such exhibition will mislead are navigator, shall be punished\nwith imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to seven\nyears, or with fine, or with both.",
    "punishment": "shall be punished\nwith imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to seven\nyears, or with fine, or with both.",
