    "id": "ppc-337-g",
    "statute": "Pakistan Penal Code 1860",
    "section": "337-G",
    "title": "Punishment for hurt by rash or negligent driving",
    "description": "Punishment for hurt by rash or negligent driving\n\nTHE PAKISTAN PENAL CODE, 1860\nTHE PAKISTAN PENAL CODE, 1860\nACT NO. XLV OF 1860.\nCHAPTER XVI OF OFFENCES AFFECTING THE HUMAN BODY\nOf Offences affecting Life\n337G.\nPunishment for hurt by rash or negligent\ndriving. Whoever causes hurt by\nrash or negligent driving shall be liable to the arsh or daman specified for the kind of hurt caused and may also be\npunished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to\nfive years as ta'zir.\nNOTES\n(a) Shajjah-i-Khafifah Hurt on head or face in which bone Daman\nand imprisonment of\nis\nnot exposed either\ndescription for two years.\n(Bailable)\n(b) Shajjah-i-mudihah Hurt in which bone is exposed but Qisas,\nArsh and imprisonment of\nnot\ndislocated either\ndescription for five years.\n(Not\nbailable)\n(c) Shajjah-i-hashimah Fracture of the bone without its Arsh, and imprisonment of either\ndislocation description\nfor seven years. (Not\nbailable)\n(d) Shajjah-i-munaqqilah Fracture of bone by dislocation Arsh, and imprisonment of either\ndescription\nfor ten years. (Not\nbailable)\n(e) Shajjah-i-ammah Fracture of the skull when the Arsh, and imprisonment of either\nwound\ntouches membrance of the description for\nten years. (Not\nbrain\nbailable)\n(f) Shajjah-i-damighah Fracture of the skull when the Arsh and imprisonment of either\nwound\nruptures the membrance, of description for fourteen years.\nthe\nbrain (Not\nbailable)\n(g) Jaifah When\nthe wound enters the body of Arsh, and imprisonment of either\nthe\ntrunk (If the wound pierces description for ten years and\nthrough\nany part of the body the punishment\nprovided for Itlafi\noffender\nshall be guilty of causing udw\nor Itlaf-i-salahiyyat-i-udw if\njaifah\nfor each of the wound caused.\n(Not bailable)\nseparately)\n(h) Ghayr-Jaifah Rupture of the skin causing Daman and imprisonment of\n(i) Damiyah bleeding either\ndescription for one year.\n(Bailable)\n(ii) Badiah Bone\nnot exposed Daman\nand imprisonment of\neither\ndescription for three\nyears.\n(Not bailable)\n(iii) Mutulahimah Lacerating the flesh Daman\nand imprisonment of\neither\ndescription for three\nyears.\n(Not bailable)\n(iv) Mudihah Exposing\nthe bone Daman and\nimprisonment of\neither\ndescription for five years\n(Not\nbailable)\n(v) Hashimah Fracture\nwithout disclosing of bone Daman and\nimprisonment of\neither\ndescription for five years\n(Not\nbailable)\n(vi) Munaqqilah Fracture and dislocation of bone Daman and imprisonment of\neither\ndescription for seven\nyears.\n(Not bailable)",
    "punishment": "shall be liable to the arsh or daman specified for the kind of hurt caused and may also be\npunished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may extend to\nfive years as ta'zir.",
    "category": "criminal",
