    "id": "ppc-338-h",
    "statute": "Pakistan Penal Code 1860",
    "section": "338-H",
    "title": "Saving",
    "description": "Saving\n\nTHE PAKISTAN PENAL CODE, 1860\nTHE PAKISTAN PENAL CODE, 1860\nACT NO. XLV OF 1860.\nCHAPTER XVI OF OFFENCES AFFECTING THE HUMAN BODY\nOf Offences affecting Life\n338H. Saving. (1) Nothing in this\nChapter, except sections 309, 310 and 338E, shall apply to cases pending before\nany Court immediately before the commencement of the Criminal Law (Second\nAmendment) Ordinance, 1990 (VII of 1990), or to the offences committed before\nsuch commencement\".\nNotes:\nOnly sections 309, 310 and 338-E\nshall apply to (i) cases pending before any Court, and (ii) offences committed\nimmediately before the commencement of the Criminal Law (Second Amendment) Ordinance,\n1990, but other provisions contained in the Chapter shall not apply either to\nthe pending cases or to the offences committed before commencement of the\nOrdinance. Neither section 309, nor section 310, nor section 338-E as\nsubstituted by both the Ordinances have any application to offences (e.g.,\nsection 302 (culpable homicide amounting to murder) which now stand substituted\nwith Islamic Penal offences) in respect of which cases are pending since before\ncommencement of Ordinance VII of 1990, to the offences committed before such\ncommencement, as there is no question of waiver of qisas in qatl-i-amd (section\n309) and compounding of Oisas in qatl-i-amd (section 310) as the\"' murder\nthen committed was not qatl-i-amd and punishment of Oisas is not to be exacted\nfor the murder.\nThe legislature should make the offences\nsubject matter of sections 299 to 338 P.P.C. as,' existing before the\nenforcement of the Criminal Law (Second Amendment) Ordinance, 1990,\ncompoundable on account of forgiveness or as the case may be by adding a new\nsection after section 345, Cr.P.C. This section should further provide (a) that\nsections 309, 310 and 323 of the Penal Code shall mutatis mutandis apply, and\n(b) that the application for leave to compound the offence is to be submitted\nto the Court before which any appeal or revision against the conviction is\npending and if no such proceedings are pending the application is to be\nsubmitted to the trial Court which passed the order of conviction and sentence.\nThis will be necessary as otherwise under the present state of law, the\ncommutation of sentence can be ordered by the Provincial or Central Government\nor Governor or President of Pakistan, and to these authorities it will not be\nadvisable to assign the job of determining the genuineness and voluntary nature\nof the composition and the adequacy or otherwise of the amount of diyat, arsh\nor daman, as well as the question whether despite composition, the convict is\nliable to be awarded as ta'zir. The cases of grant of pardon in the case of death sentence contemplated by the newly added\nproviso to section 381 CrP.C. can also be included for reference and decision\nto the trial Court which had awarded the death sentence. It may be noted that\nthough provision to the effect that:\n\"Provided that the sentence of death\nshall not be executed if the heirs of the\ndeceased pardon the convict or enter into a compromise with him even at the\nlast moment before execution of the sentence.\"\nhas been added to section 381, Cr.P.C. but\nthe mechanism to operate the said provision has not been provided. The afore\nnoted features and suggestions, we have ventured to make the Ordinance I of\n1991 or similar legislation, \"as to go adtore the National Assembly\nand Senate for enacting a permanent law on the subject or otherwise the\nInjunctions of Islam as contained in\nthe Qur'an and Sunnah, relating to the offence of Qatl and Jurh (Hurt) are to\nbe treated as law in force. PLD 1991 Lah. 346; PLD 1990 SC 472 ref. In Safdar\nAli's case (PLD 1991 SC 202) the Hon'ble Supreme Court observed:\n'A perusal of the above provisions indicates\nthat the waiver or the compounding of an\noffence in cases falling under section 309 (waiver-Afw of qisas in qatl-i-amd)\nand section 310 (Compounding of Qisas (Sulah) in Qatl-i-Amd) is possible even\nin those cases of qatl",
