    "title": "Attempt to commit robbery",
    "description": "Attempt to commit robbery\n\nTHE PAKISTAN PENAL CODE, 1860\nTHE PAKISTAN PENAL CODE, 1860\nACT NO. XLV OF 1860.\nCHAPTER XVII OF OFFENCES AGAINST\nPROPERTY\nOf Robbery and Dacoity\n395. Punishment for dacoity. Whoever commits dacoity shall be punished\nwith imprisonment for life or with rigorous imprisonment for a term which [ Subs. by Ordinance III of 1980, dated\n3.2.1980.][shall not be less than four years nor more than] ten years and shall\nalso be liable to fine.\nNotes: Evidence through identification. Not a substantive piece of evidence\nbut a corroborative. 1989 P.Cr.L.J. 2227. Recovery not inspiring confidence.\n1989 P.Cr.L.J. 2227. Ocular account corroborated by evidence of identification\nparade. NLR 1991 Cr.L.J. 794. One circumstance creating a reasonable doubt.\n1991 P.Cr.L.J. 1216.",
