    "description": "Lurking house-trespass or house breaking in order to commit offence punishable with imprisonment\n\nTHE PAKISTAN PENAL CODE, 1860\nTHE PAKISTAN PENAL CODE, 1860\nACT NO. XLV OF 1860.\nCHAPTER XVII OF OFFENCES AGAINST\nPROPERTY\nOf Fraudulent Deeds and Dispossession of\nProperty\n454. Lurking house-trespass or house-breaking in order to commit offence\npunishable with imprisonment. Whoever commits lurking house-trespass\nor house breaking, in order to committing of any offence punishable with\nimprisonment, shall be punished with imprisonment of either description for a\nterm which may extend to three years, and shall also be liable to fine; and if\nthe offence intended to be committed is theft, the term of the imprisonment may\nbe extended to ten years.",
