    "section": "462",
    "title": "Dishonestly breaking open receptacle containing property when committed by person entrusted with custody",
    "description": "Dishonestly breaking open receptacle containing property when committed by person entrusted with custody\n\nTHE PAKISTAN PENAL CODE, 1860\nTHE PAKISTAN PENAL CODE, 1860\nACT NO. XLV OF 1860.\nCHAPTER XVII OF OFFENCES AGAINST\nPROPERTY\nOf Fraudulent Deeds and Dispossession of\nProperty\n462. Punishment for same offence when\ncommitted by person entrusted with\ncustody. Whoever, being entrusted with any closed receptacle which\ncontains or which he believes to\ncontain property, without having authority to open the same, dishonestly, or\nwith intent to commit mischief, breaks opens receptacle, shall be or unfastens\nthat punished with imprisonment of either description for a term which may\nextend to three years, or with fine, or with both.",
