    "title": "Offences not punishable with death",
    "description": "Offences not punishable with death\n\nTHE CODE OF CRIMINAL PROCEDURE (ACT V OF 1898)\nTHE CODE OF CRIMINAL PROCEDURE (ACT V OF 1898)\nCHAPTER III POWERS OF\nCOURTS\nA. Description of offences cognizable by each Court\n30. Offences not punishable with death. In the Punjab, the\nNorth-West Frontier, in Sind and in those parts of the Provinces in which there\nare Deputy Commissioners or Assistant Commissioners the Provincial Government\nmay, notwithstanding anything contained in section 29, invest the District\nMagistrate or any Magistrate of the first class, with power to try as a\nMagistrate all offences not punishable with death.",
