    "title": "Sentence which Magistrate may pass",
    "description": "Sentence which Magistrate may pass\n\nTHE CODE OF CRIMINAL PROCEDURE (ACT V OF 1898)\nTHE CODE OF CRIMINAL PROCEDURE (ACT V OF 1898)\nCHAPTER III POWERS OF\nCOURTS\nB. Sentences which may be passed Courts of various Classes\n32. Sentence which Magistrate may pass. (1) The Courts of\nMagistrates may pass the following sentences namely:\n(a) Courts of Magistrates\nof Imprisonment for a term not exceeding\nthree\nthe first class\n; years, including such solitary\nconfinement as is\nauthorized\nby law; Fine not exceeding [fifteen]5\nthousand\nrupees arsh, daman Whipping.\n(b) Courts of Magistrates of Imprisonment\nfor a term not exceeding one year\nthe second class; including such solitary confinement as is\nauthorized\nby law; Fine not exceeding (five)7\nthousand\nrupees.\n(c) Courts of Magistrates of Imprisonment\nfor a term not exceeding one\nthe third class; month; Fine not exceeding (one thousand)8\nrupees.\n(2) The Courts of any\nMagistrate may pass any lawful sentence, combining any of the sentences which\nit is authorized by law to passs.",
