    "title": "Additional powers conferrable on Magistrates",
    "description": "Additional powers conferrable on Magistrates\n\nTHE CODE OF CRIMINAL PROCEDURE (ACT V OF 1898)\nTHE CODE OF CRIMINAL PROCEDURE (ACT V OF 1898)\nCHAPTER III POWERS OF\nCOURTS\nC. Ordinary and Additional Powers\n37. Additional powers conferrable on Magistrates. In addition to\nhis ordinary powers, any Sub-divisional Magistrate or any Magistrate of the\nfirst, second or third class may be invested by the Provincial Government or\nthe District Magistrate, case may be, with an as the by powers specified in the\nfourth schedule as powers with which he may be invested by the Provincial\nGovernment or the District Magistrate.",
