    "statute": "Criminal Procedure Code Cr P C 1898",
    "section": "543",
    "title": "Interpreter to be bound to interpret truthfully",
    "description": "Interpreter to be bound to interpret truthfully\n\nTHE CODE OF CRIMINAL PROCEDURE (ACT V OF 1898)\nTHE CODE OF CRIMINAL PROCEDURE (ACT V OF 1898)\nPART IX\nSUPPLEMENTARY PROVISIONS\nCHAPTER XLVI\nMISCELLANEOUS\n543. Interpreter to be bound to interpret truthfully. When the\nservices of an interpreter are required by any Criminal Court for the\ninterpretation of any evidence or statement, he shall be bound to state the\ntrue interpretation of such evidence or statement.",
