    "id": "companies-ordinance-258",
    "statute": "Companies Ordinance 1984",
    "section": "258",
    "title": "Audit of cost accounts",
    "description": "Audit of cost accounts\n\nCOMPANIES ORDINANCE 1984\nCOMPANIES\nORDINANCE 1984\n(ORDINANCE NO. XLVII OF 1984)\n[8th October, 1984]\nAn Ordinance to consolidate and\namend the law relating to companies and certain other associations.\nPART VIII.- AUDIT\n258. Audit of cost accounts.--(1) Where any company or class of\ncompanies is required under clause (e) of subsection (1) of section 230 to\ninclude in its books of account the particulars referred to therein, the\nFederal Government may direct that an audit of cost accounts of the company\nshall be conducted in such manner and with such stipulations as may be\nspecified in the order by an auditor who is a chartered accountant within the\nmeaning of the Chartered Accountants Ordinance, 1961 (X of 1961), or a cost and\nmanagement accountant within the meaning of the Cost and Management Accountants\nAct, 1966 (XIV of 1966); and such auditor shall have the same powers, duties\nand liabilites as an auditor of a company and such other powers, duties and\nliabilities as may be prescribed.",
