    "id": "companies-ordinance-259",
    "statute": "Companies Ordinance 1984",
    "section": "259",
    "title": "Penalty for non-compliance with provisions by companies",
    "description": "Penalty for non-compliance with provisions by companies\n\nCOMPANIES ORDINANCE 1984\nCOMPANIES\nORDINANCE 1984\n(ORDINANCE NO. XLVII OF 1984)\n[8th October, 1984]\nAn Ordinance to consolidate and\namend the law relating to companies and certain other associations.\nPART VIII.- AUDIT\n259. Penalty for non-compliance with provisions by companies.--If\ndefault is made by a company in complying with any of the provisions of\nsections 252 to 254 or 256 to 258, the company and every officer of the company\nwho is knowingly and wilfully a party to the default shall be punishable with\nfine which may extend to two thousand rupees\nfifty thousand rupees and in the case of continuing\ndefault to a further fine which may extend to two thousand rupees for every day\nafter the first during which the default continues.\n* Above Amendment has been made According to the Companies Amendment Ordinance 2002",
