    "title": "Power to fill vacancy in office of liquidator",
    "description": "Power to fill vacancy in office of liquidator\n\nCOMPANIES ORDINANCE 1984\nCOMPANIES\nORDINANCE 1984\n(ORDINANCE NO. XLVII OF 1984)\n[8th October, 1984]\nAn Ordinance to consolidate and\namend the law relating to companies and certain other associations.\nPART XI. VOLUNTARY WINDING UP\nPROVISIONS APPLICABLE TO CREDITORS' VOLUNTARY WINDING UP\n379. Power to fill vacancy in office of liquidator.\u2011\u2011If\na vacancy occurs, by death, resignation or otherwise, in the office of a\nliquidator, other than a liquidator appointed by or by the direction of, the\nCourt, the creditors in general meeting may fill the vacancy by appointing a\nperson who has given his written consent to act as liquidator, and for this\npurpose the provisions of section 365 shall mutatis mutandis apply.",
