    "id": "companies-ordinance-386",
    "statute": "Companies Ordinance 1984",
    "section": "386",
    "title": "Application of sections 328 and 329 to voluntary winding up",
    "description": "Application of sections 328 and 329 to voluntary winding up\n\nCOMPANIES ORDINANCE 1984\nCOMPANIES\nORDINANCE 1984\n(ORDINANCE NO. XLVII OF 1984)\n[8th October, 1984]\nAn Ordinance to consolidate and\namend the law relating to companies and certain other associations.\nPART XI. VOLUNTARY WINDING UP\nPROVISIONS APPLICABLE TO EVERY VOLUNTARY WINDING UP\n386. Application of sections 328 and 329 to voluntary winding up.\u2011\u2011The\nprovisions of sections 328 and 329 shall, so far as may be, apply to every\nvoluntary winding up as they apply to winding up by the Court except that\nreferences to\u2011\u2011\n(a) 'the Court\" shall be\nomitted;\n(b) the \"official\nliquidator\" or the \"provisional manager\" shall be construed as\nreferences to the liquidator; and\n(c) the \"relevant date\"\nshall be construed as reference to the date of commencement of the winding up;\nand\nthe report referred to in section\n329 shall be submitted to the registrar instead of the Court",
