    "statute": "Negotiable Instruments Act 1881",
    "section": "69",
    "title": "Instrument payable at specified place",
    "description": "Instrument payable at specified place\n\nCHAPTER V\nCHAPTER V\nOF PRESENTMENT\n69. Instrument\npayable at specified place. A promissory note or bill or exchange made,\ndrawn or accepted payable at a specified place must, in order to charge the\nmaker or drawer thereof, be presented for payment at that place.",
    "punishment": null,
