    "statute": "Arbitration Act 1940",
    "section": "23",
    "title": "Order of reference",
    "description": "Order of reference\n\nCHAPTER IV\nTHE ARBITRATION ACT, 1940\n(X OF 1940)\n[11 March, 1940]\nAn\nAct to consolidate and amend the law relating to Arbitration.\nWHERE it is\nexpedient to consolidate and amend. the law relating to arbitration in\nPakistan.\nIt is hereby\nenacted as follows:\u2011\nCHAPTER IV\nARBITRATION\nIN SUITS\n23.\nOrder of reference. (1) The Court shall, by order, refer to the arbitrator\nthe matter in difference which he is required to determine, and shall in the\norder specify such time as it thinks reasonable for the making of the award.\n(2)\nWhere a matter is referred to arbitration the Court shall not, save in the\nmanner and to the extent provided in this Act, deal with such matter in the\nsuit.",
