    "id": "registration-act-3",
    "statute": "Registration Act 1908",
    "section": "3",
    "title": "Of the registration establishment",
    "description": "Of the registration establishment\n\nTHE REGISTRATION ACT 1908\nTHE REGISTRATION ACT 1908\n(XVI OF 1908)\n[18th December,\n1908]\nAn Act to\nconsolidate the enactments relating to the Registration of Document\nFor Statement of Objects and\nReasons, see Gazette of India, 1908. Pt. V. p. 325; for Report of Select\nCommittee, see i6 id, 1908, Pt. V, p. 387; and for Proceeding\u2011in -\nCouncil, see ibid, 1908, Pt. VI, pp. 148, 154 and 182.\nWHEREAS it is\nexpedient to consolidate the enactments relating to the registration of\ndocuments:\nIt is hereby\nenacted as follows:\u2011\u2011\nPART II\nOF THE REGISTRATION ESTABLISHMENT\n3. Inspector\u2011General\nof Registration. (1) The Provincial Government\nshall appoint an officer to be the Inspector\u2011General of Registration for\nthe territories subject to such Government;\nProvided that\nthe Provincial Government may, instead of making such appointment, direct that\nall or any of the powers and duties hereinafter conferred and imposed upon the\nInspector\u2011General shall be exercised and performed by such office or\nofficers, \u2011and within such local limits, as the Provincial Government\nappoints in this behalf.\n(2) Any\nInspector\u2011General may hold simultaneously any other office in the service\nof the State.\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000",
