    "id": "registration-act-7",
    "statute": "Registration Act 1908",
    "section": "7",
    "title": "Offices of registrar and sub-registrar",
    "description": "Offices of registrar and sub-registrar\n\nTHE REGISTRATION ACT 1908\nTHE REGISTRATION ACT 1908\n(XVI OF 1908)\n[18th December,\n1908]\nAn Act to\nconsolidate the enactments relating to the Registration of Document\nFor Statement of Objects and\nReasons, see Gazette of India, 1908. Pt. V. p. 325; for Report of Select\nCommittee, see i6 id, 1908, Pt. V, p. 387; and for Proceeding\u2011in -\nCouncil, see ibid, 1908, Pt. VI, pp. 148, 154 and 182.\nWHEREAS it is\nexpedient to consolidate the enactments relating to the registration of\ndocuments:\nIt is hereby\nenacted as follows:\u2011\u2011\nPART II\nOF THE REGISTRATION ESTABLISHMENT\n7. Offices of\nRegistrar and Sub\u2011Registrar. (1) The\nProvincial Government shall establish in every district an office to be styled\nthe offices of the Registrar and in every sub\u2011district an office or\nofficers to be styled the office of the Sub\u2011Registrar or the offices of\nthe Joint Sub\u2011Registrars.\n(2) The\nProvincial Government may amalgamate with any office of a Registrar any office\nof a Sub\u2011Registrar subordinate to such Registrar, and may authorize any\nSub\u2011Registrar whose office has been so amalgamated to exercise and\nperform, in addition to his own powers and duties all or any of the powers and\nduties of the Registrar, to whom he Is subordinate:\nProvided that no\nsuch authorization shall enable a Sub\u2011Registrar to hear an appeal against\nan order passed by himself under this Act.\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000",
