    "id": "registration-act-10",
    "statute": "Registration Act 1908",
    "section": "10",
    "title": "Absence of registrar of vacancy in his office",
    "description": "Absence of registrar of vacancy in his office\n\nTHE REGISTRATION ACT 1908\nTHE REGISTRATION ACT 1908\n(XVI OF 1908)\n[18th December,\n1908]\nAn Act to\nconsolidate the enactments relating to the Registration of Document\nFor Statement of Objects and\nReasons, see Gazette of India, 1908. Pt. V. p. 325; for Report of Select\nCommittee, see i6 id, 1908, Pt. V, p. 387; and for Proceeding\u2011in -\nCouncil, see ibid, 1908, Pt. VI, pp. 148, 154 and 182.\nWHEREAS it is\nexpedient to consolidate the enactments relating to the registration of\ndocuments:\nIt is hereby\nenacted as follows:\u2011\u2011\nPART II\nOF THE REGISTRATION ESTABLISHMENT\n10. Absence\nof Registrar or vacancy in his office. (1) When any\nRegistrar is absent otherwise than on duty in his district, or when his office\nis temporarily vacant, any person whom the Inspector\u2011General appoints in\nthis behalf, or, in default of such appointment, the Judge of the District\nCourt within the local limits of whose jurisdiction the Registrar's office is\nsituate, shall be the Registrar during such absence or until the Provincial\nGovernment fills up the vacancy.\n(2) [Omitted by\nthe A0. 1949.]\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000",
