    "id": "registration-act-19",
    "statute": "Registration Act 1908",
    "section": "19",
    "title": "Document in language not understood by registering officer",
    "description": "Document in language not understood by registering officer\n\nTHE REGISTRATION ACT 1908\nTHE REGISTRATION ACT 1908\n(XVI OF 1908)\n[18th December,\n1908]\nAn Act to\nconsolidate the enactments relating to the Registration of Document\nFor Statement of Objects and\nReasons, see Gazette of India, 1908. Pt. V. p. 325; for Report of Select\nCommittee, see i6 id, 1908, Pt. V, p. 387; and for Proceeding\u2011in -\nCouncil, see ibid, 1908, Pt. VI, pp. 148, 154 and 182.\nWHEREAS it is\nexpedient to consolidate the enactments relating to the registration of\ndocuments:\nIt is hereby\nenacted as follows:\u2011\u2011\nPART III\nOF REGISTRABLE DOCUMENTS\n19. Document\nin language not understood by registering officer. If\nany document duly presented for registration be in a language which the\nregistering officer does not understand, and which is not, commonly used in the\ndistrict, he shall refuse to register the document, unless it be accompanied by\na true translation into a language commonly used in the district and also by a\ntrue copy.\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000",
