    "id": "registration-act-70",
    "statute": "Registration Act 1908",
    "section": "70",
    "title": "Power of inspector-general to remit fines",
    "description": "Power of inspector-general to remit fines\n\nTHE REGISTRATION ACT 1908\nTHE REGISTRATION ACT 1908\n(XVI OF 1908)\n[18th December,\n1908]\nAn Act to\nconsolidate the enactments relating to the Registration of Document\nFor Statement of Objects and\nReasons, see Gazette of India, 1908. Pt. V. p. 325; for Report of Select\nCommittee, see i6 id, 1908, Pt. V, p. 387; and for Proceeding\u2011in -\nCouncil, see ibid, 1908, Pt. VI, pp. 148, 154 and 182.\nWHEREAS it is\nexpedient to consolidate the enactments relating to the registration of\ndocuments:\nIt is hereby\nenacted as follows:\u2011\u2011\nPART XI\nOF THE DUTIES AND POWERS OF REGISTERING OFFICERS\n(E) Of the\nControlling Powers of Registrars and Inspectors-Genera\n70. Power of\nInspector-General to remit fines. The\nInspector-General may also, in the exercise of his discretion, remit wholly or\nin part the difference between any fine levied under section 25 or section 34,\nand the amount of the proper registration fee.\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000",
