    "id": "registration-act-70-c",
    "statute": "Registration Act 1908",
    "section": "70-C",
    "title": "Appointment of photo-registrars",
    "description": "Appointment of photo-registrars\n\nTHE REGISTRATION ACT 1908\nTHE REGISTRATION ACT 1908\n(XVI OF 1908)\n[18th December,\n1908]\nAn Act to\nconsolidate the enactments relating to the Registration of Document\nFor Statement of Objects and\nReasons, see Gazette of India, 1908. Pt. V. p. 325; for Report of Select\nCommittee, see i6 id, 1908, Pt. V, p. 387; and for Proceeding\u2011in -\nCouncil, see ibid, 1908, Pt. VI, pp. 148, 154 and 182.\nWHEREAS it is\nexpedient to consolidate the enactments relating to the registration of\ndocuments:\nIt is hereby\nenacted as follows:\u2011\u2011\nPART XI-A\nOF THE COPYING OF DOCUMENTS BY MEAN OF PHOTOGRAPHY\nPart XI-A\ninst. by the Registration (Amendment) Ordinance XXXXV of 1 962; S. 11\n70-C.\nAppointment of Photo-Registrar. The Provincial\nGovernment may appoint a Registrar or Sub-Registrar or any other person to be a\nPhoto-Registrar for the performance of duties under this Part:\nProvided that\nthe Provincial Government may subject to such restrictions and conditions as it\nthinks fit, delegate the power of appointing Photo-Registrar to the\nInspector-General of Registration.\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000",
