    "id": "registration-act-70-d",
    "statute": "Registration Act 1908",
    "section": "70-D",
    "title": "Documents may be photographed in areas notified by Government",
    "description": "Documents may be photographed in areas notified by Government\n\nTHE REGISTRATION ACT 1908\nTHE REGISTRATION ACT 1908\n(XVI OF 1908)\n[18th December,\n1908]\nAn Act to\nconsolidate the enactments relating to the Registration of Document\nFor Statement of Objects and\nReasons, see Gazette of India, 1908. Pt. V. p. 325; for Report of Select\nCommittee, see i6 id, 1908, Pt. V, p. 387; and for Proceeding\u2011in -\nCouncil, see ibid, 1908, Pt. VI, pp. 148, 154 and 182.\nWHEREAS it is\nexpedient to consolidate the enactments relating to the registration of\ndocuments:\nIt is hereby\nenacted as follows:\u2011\u2011\nPART XI-A\nOF THE COPYING OF DOCUMENTS BY MEAN OF PHOTOGRAPHY\nPart XI-A\ninst. by the Registration (Amendment) Ordinance XXXXV of 1 962; S. 11\n70-D.\nDocuments may be photographed in areas notified by Government. (1) The Provincial Government may, by notification in the official\nGazette, direct that in any district or sub-district specified in the\nnotification copies of documents admitted to registration under this Act shall\nbe made by means of photography.\n(2) On the issue\nof such notification it shall be translated into urdu and shall be posted in a\nconspicuous place at the Registration offices affected by the notification.\nWords\nomitted by the President Adaptation of Laws Order, 4 of 1975.\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000",
