    "id": "registration-act-72",
    "statute": "Registration Act 1908",
    "section": "72",
    "title": "Appeal to registrar from orders of sub-registrar refusing registration on ground other than denial of execution",
    "description": "Appeal to registrar from orders of sub-registrar refusing registration on ground other than denial of execution\n\nTHE REGISTRATION ACT 1908\nTHE REGISTRATION ACT 1908\n(XVI OF 1908)\n[18th December,\n1908]\nAn Act to\nconsolidate the enactments relating to the Registration of Document\nFor Statement of Objects and\nReasons, see Gazette of India, 1908. Pt. V. p. 325; for Report of Select\nCommittee, see i6 id, 1908, Pt. V, p. 387; and for Proceeding\u2011in -\nCouncil, see ibid, 1908, Pt. VI, pp. 148, 154 and 182.\nWHEREAS it is\nexpedient to consolidate the enactments relating to the registration of\ndocuments:\nIt is hereby\nenacted as follows:\u2011\u2011\nPART XII\nOF REFUSAL TO REGISTER\n72. Appeal to\nRegistrar from orders of Sub\u2011Registrar refusing registration on ground\nother than denial of execution. (1) Except where\nthe refusal is made on the ground of denial of execution, an appeal shall lie\nagainst an order of a Sub\u2011Registrar refusing to admit a document to\nregistration (whether the registration of such document is compulsory or\noptional) to the Registrar to whom such Sub\u2011Registrar is subordinate, if\npresented to such Registrar within thirty days from the date of the order; and\nthe Registrar may reverse or alter such order.\n(2) If the order\nof the Registrar directs the document to he registered and the document is duly\npresented for registration within thirty days after the snaking of such order,\nthe Sub\u2011Registrar shall obey the same, and thereupon, shall, so' far as\nmay be practicable, follow the procedure prescribed in sections 58, 59 and 60;\nand such registration shall that, effect as if the document had been registered\nwhen it was first duly presented for registration.\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000",
