    "id": "registration-act-76",
    "statute": "Registration Act 1908",
    "section": "76",
    "title": "Order of refusal by registrar",
    "description": "Order of refusal by registrar\n\nTHE REGISTRATION ACT 1908\nTHE REGISTRATION ACT 1908\n(XVI OF 1908)\n[18th December,\n1908]\nAn Act to\nconsolidate the enactments relating to the Registration of Document\nFor Statement of Objects and\nReasons, see Gazette of India, 1908. Pt. V. p. 325; for Report of Select\nCommittee, see i6 id, 1908, Pt. V, p. 387; and for Proceeding\u2011in -\nCouncil, see ibid, 1908, Pt. VI, pp. 148, 154 and 182.\nWHEREAS it is\nexpedient to consolidate the enactments relating to the registration of\ndocuments:\nIt is hereby\nenacted as follows:\u2011\u2011\nPART XII\nOF REFUSAL TO REGISTER\n76. Order of\nrefusal by Registrar. (1) Every Registrar refusing\u2011\u2011\n(a) to register\na document except on the ground that the property to which it relates is not\nsituate within his district or that the document ought to be registered in the\noffice of a Sub\u2011Registrar; or\n(b) to direct\nthe registration of a document under section 72 or section 75,\u2011\u2011\nshall make an\norder of refusal and record the reasons for such order in his Book No. 2 and,\nun application made by any person executing or claiming under the document,\nshall, without unnecessary delay, give him a copy of the reasons so recorded.\n(2) No appeal\nlies from any order by a Registrar under this section of section 72.\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000",
