    "id": "registration-act-87",
    "statute": "Registration Act 1908",
    "section": "87",
    "title": "Nothing so done invalidated by defect in appointment or procedure",
    "description": "Nothing so done invalidated by defect in appointment or procedure\n\nTHE REGISTRATION ACT 1908\nTHE REGISTRATION ACT 1908\n(XVI OF 1908)\n[18th December,\n1908]\nAn Act to\nconsolidate the enactments relating to the Registration of Document\nFor Statement of Objects and\nReasons, see Gazette of India, 1908. Pt. V. p. 325; for Report of Select\nCommittee, see i6 id, 1908, Pt. V, p. 387; and for Proceeding\u2011in -\nCouncil, see ibid, 1908, Pt. VI, pp. 148, 154 and 182.\nWHEREAS it is\nexpedient to consolidate the enactments relating to the registration of\ndocuments:\nIt is hereby\nenacted as follows:\u2011\u2011\nPART XV\nMISCELLANEOUS\n87. Nothing\nso done invalidated by defect in appointment or procedure. (1) Nothing done in good faith pursuant to this Act or any Act\nhereby repealed, by any registering officer, shall be deemed invalid merely by\nreason of any defect in his appointment or procedure.\n(2) Any defect\nin or the want of authority of a person to present a document shall not be\nitself, render invalid the registration of the document or the transaction\neffected by it.\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000\n\u0000",
    "punishment": null,
    "category": "commercial",
    "isMajorCode": true
