    "title": "Rules for supply, number, renewal and keeping accounts of stamps",
    "description": "Rules for supply, number, renewal and keeping accounts of stamps\n\nTHE COUR FEES ACT 1870\nTHE COUR FEES ACT 1870\nACT No. VII of 1870\n[11th March, 1870]\nCHAPTER V\nOF THE MODE OF LEVYING FEES\n27. Rules for supply, number, renewal and keeping\naccounts of stamps. The (Subs. by A. O., 1937, for \"L. G\n\". For definition of \"Appropriate, Govt.\", see s. IA, supra.) [Appropriate Government] may, from\ntime to time, make (For rules under s. 27, see different Local Rules and Orders.)rules for regulating\u2011\n(a) the supply\nof stamps to be used under this Act ;\n(b) the number\nof stamps to be used for denoting any fee chargeable under this Act ;\n(c) the renewal\nof damaged or spoiled stamps ; and\n(d) the keeping\naccounts of all stamps used under this Act\nProvided that,\nin the case of stamps used under section 3 in a High Court, such rules shall be\nmade with the concurrence of the Chief Justice of such Court.\nAll such rules\nshall be published in the (Subs. by A. O., 1937, for \"local official Gazette\n\".) [official Gazette],\nand shall thereupon have the force of law.",
