    "title": "Sale of stamps",
    "description": "Sale of stamps\n\nTHE COUR FEES ACT 1870\nTHE COUR FEES ACT 1870\nACT No. VII of 1870\n[11th March, 1870]\nCHAPTER VI\nMISCELLANEOUS\n34. Sale of stamps. (Subs. for the original section by the Amending Act, 1891 (12\nof 1891).) [34.\u2011(1) The (Subs. by A. O., 1937, for \"L. G.\". For definition\nof \" Appropriate Government \"sees. IA, supra.) [Appropriate Government] may from\ntime to time make (For rules issued under this section, see different Local\nRules and Orders\u2011\nFor rules framed by the Government of East Bengal, see Dacca\nGazette Ext., dated the 6th October, 1948, Pt. I, and ibid., 1950, Pt. I, pp.\n902\u20113.)rules for regulating the sale of stamps to be used under this Act,\nthe persons by whom alone such sale is to be conducted, and the duties and\nremuneration of such persons.\n(2) All such\nrules shall be published in the (Subs. by A. O., 1937, for \" local official Gazette\n\".) [official Gazette],\nand shall thereupon have the force of law.\n(3) Any person\nappointed to sell stamps who disobeys any rule made under this section, and any\nperson not so appointed who sells or offers for sale any stamp, shall be\npunished with im prisonment for a term which may extend to six months, or with\nfine which may extend to five hundred rupees, or with both.]",
