    "statute": "General Clauses Act 1897",
    "section": "5",
    "title": "Coming into operation of enactments",
    "description": "Coming into operation of enactments\n\nTHE GENERAL CLAUSES ACT\nTHE GENERAL CLAUSES ACT\n(X of 1897)\nGENERAL RULES OF\nCONSTRUCTIONS\n5. Coming into operation of enactments: (1) Where any Central Act is not expressed\nto come into operation on any particular day, then it shall come into operation\non the day on which it receives the assent:\u2011\u2011\n(a) in\nthe case of a Central Act made before the twenty\u2011third day of March,\n1956, of the Governor\u2011General; and\n(b) in\nthe case of a Central Act made after that date, of the President.\n(2) Omitted by AO. 1961 Art. 2 and Sch.\n(with effect from the 23rd March, 1956).\n(3) Unless the contrary is expressed, a\nCentral Act. or Regulation shall be construed as coming into operation\nimmediately on the expiration of the day preceding its commencement.",
